{
  "about": "How a later milestone puts a new tool under the golden replay. A rule turns the recorded commands of one old command into calls of the new tool. Two kinds of rule. (1) No 'agree': the answer must be the baseline's (rows as sets where the SQL has no ORDER BY). Run with: sfsharness replay compare --translated. (2) With 'agree': the new tool's answer has another shape, so the two are held against each other on what both give, by the comparison named (Agree.cs: find-names, loadorder-header, loadorder-stats, loadorder-order; record-old for Inspect, Dump, Read and Live against sfs_record: which record, its EditorID, its type, the plugin it was read from; record-values: every value today's Dump or Live shows is in sfs_record's JSON; refs-old and refs-live for Refs and Live --refs against sfs_refs: the records that point at the target, the plugin each was read from, their fields and how many links each has. Every refs comparison is also asked with search: bytes, and the link index and the byte search must give the same rows. A record only sfs_refs lists is checked through today's Live --links). Run with: sfsharness agree (it is also a part of sfsharness all). A recorded command with no rule runs as it was recorded: that is the test of the old names on the new engine (milestone M9), and needs no rule. 'command' is the old command's name. 'when' (optional) is a pattern the joined arguments must match. 'options' are the old command's options that take a value. In 'params', \"{1}\" is the first plain argument, \"{*}\" every plain argument joined by spaces, \"{--in}\" an option's value (left out when the command didn't have it), \"{?--csv}\" true when the flag was given, \"{args}\" every argument as a list. 'via' is service (the default) or mcp. 'also' lists old commands that weren't recorded but must agree with a new tool: each is asked both ways. 'explained' lists every accepted disagreement: 'agree' is the comparison, 'match' a pattern on the disagreement's line, 'why' says which side is right and how that was checked against the plugin. A disagreement that matches no entry fails the run. The rule under 'example' is not used: it shows the shape of kind (1).",
  "rules": [
    { "command": "names", "options": [ "--in", "--maxwidth" ], "tool": "sfs_find", "params": { "query": "{*}", "in": "{--in}", "limit": 2000 }, "agree": "find-names" },
    { "command": "header", "tool": "sfs_loadorder", "params": { "view": "plugin", "plugin": "{1}" }, "agree": "loadorder-header" },
    { "command": "stats", "tool": "sfs_loadorder", "params": { "view": "plugin", "plugin": "{1}" }, "agree": "loadorder-stats" },
    { "command": "inspect", "when": "^\\S+ \\S+( --\\S+ \\S+)*$", "options": [ "--maxwidth" ], "tool": "sfs_record", "params": { "record": "{2}", "plugin": "{1}" }, "agree": "record-old" },
    { "command": "inspect", "when": "^\\S+ \\S+ \\S+( --\\S+ \\S+)*$", "options": [ "--maxwidth" ], "tool": "sfs_record", "params": { "record": "{3}", "plugin": "{1}" }, "agree": "record-old" },
    { "command": "dump", "when": "^\\S+ \\S+( --\\S+ \\S+)*$", "options": [ "--maxwidth" ], "tool": "sfs_record", "params": { "record": "{2}", "plugin": "{1}", "view": "json" }, "agree": "record-old" },
    { "command": "read", "when": "^\\S+( \\S+)?( --\\S+ \\S+)*$", "options": [ "--maxwidth" ], "tool": "sfs_record", "params": { "record": "{2}", "plugin": "{1}" }, "agree": "record-old" },
    { "command": "refs", "options": [ "--in", "--maxwidth" ], "tool": "sfs_refs", "params": { "record": "{1}", "in": "{--in}", "world": true, "limit": 2000 }, "agree": "refs-old" }
  ],
  "also": [
    { "id": "lo-all", "old": [ "LoadOrder", "--all" ], "tool": "sfs_loadorder", "params": { "view": "order", "all": true, "limit": 2000 }, "agree": "loadorder-order" },
    { "id": "lo-loaded", "old": [ "LoadOrder", "--quick" ], "tool": "sfs_loadorder", "params": { "view": "order", "limit": 2000 }, "agree": "loadorder-order" },
    { "id": "v01", "old": ["Dump", "Starfield.esm", "00424E:Starfield.esm"], "tool": "sfs_record", "params": {"record": "00424E:Starfield.esm", "plugin": "Starfield.esm", "view": "json", "max_chars": 8000000}, "agree": "record-values" },
